      "ref": "main",
      "sha256": "230276c610b8cb49fea9f6c1be4f7a2db82197c0bc80d33d1e5288d31787b225",
      "_comment": "Native desktop runner scaffolding for Windows builds. The SDK's app_type.supacharge block installs windows/ into the host with ${package}-parameterized naming (supacharge.exe, CMake project name, window title, exe metadata). Supacharge's repo already carries its own windows/ tree - the historical source of these templates - which the installer's host-file guard leaves untouched. The build_windows CI flag stays host-side in supacharge (workflows cannot be SDK-installed - the CI guard blocks workflow deploys). Mirrors manager.json/pos.json."
    }
  ],
  "host_routes": [
    {
      "path": "/onboarding-intro",
      "page": "OnboardingRoute.page",
      "type": "MaterialRoute",
      "import": "package:${package}/presentation/routes/onboarding_route_pages.dart",
      "_comment": "Host composition file (imports lms_sdk directly, so ADR-005 forbids it living inside any single SDK's lib/) — Supacharge's onboarding-carousel entry surface. auth_sdk's login/register/reset routes are NOT here — auth_sdk now owns them directly via its own manifest + templated auth_route_pages.dart, installed automatically into every app that installs auth_sdk."
    }
  ]
